PROMPT 1 — ROUTELESS PROJECT FOUNDATION
ROLE

Act as a senior full-stack engineer, software architect and UI/UX designer.

Build the foundation of ROUTELESS — The Last Mile, an integrated rural transportation management platform connecting rural students to schools and colleges.

OBJECTIVE

Create a complete, runnable React application with a professional design system, modular architecture and navigation for five user interfaces:

Student Dashboard
Driver Dashboard
Smart Touchscreen Kiosk
Admin Verification Panel
Crisis Control Center
TECHNOLOGY
React
Vite
TypeScript
Tailwind CSS
React Router
Lucide icons
Vitest
Playwright
REQUIREMENTS
Inspect the existing project before making changes.
Establish a clean modular project structure.
Create responsive layouts for desktop, tablet and mobile.
Create a consistent ROUTELESS design system.
Implement role-based demo navigation.
Create separate layouts for students, drivers, admins and kiosks.
Implement a dashboard overview with demonstration statistics.
Add loading, empty, error and offline states.
Create reusable cards, tables, forms, navigation and status badges.
Use fictional demonstration data.
Never claim demo authentication is real identity verification.
Do not leave visible buttons inactive.
DESIGN

Use a professional blue, white, green and neutral-grey colour palette.

The application must look like a real transportation management product, not a generic template.

DIRECTORY STRUCTURE

Create an organized structure containing:

src/components
src/pages
src/layouts
src/data
src/services
src/hooks
src/types
src/utils
src/styles
src/tests
public
ACCEPTANCE TESTS
Application starts successfully.
All five interfaces are accessible.
Navigation works.
Responsive layouts work.
Shared components are reusable.
No major console errors.
Demo information is clearly labelled.
EXECUTION

Build the actual application, not just an architecture document.

At completion, report the files created, features implemented, test results and instructions for continuing with Prompt 2.

Preserve the project for subsequent prompts.
